WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:08.509 --> 00:00:13.514
16 September. in the
year of our lord 1702.

2
00:00:14.348 --> 00:00:16.892
The wind has favored us on my journey.

3
00:00:17.768 --> 00:00:20.771
The crew informs me
we are soon to make port.

4
00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:24.024
I hear he is a great man.

5
00:00:24.525 --> 00:00:28.070
Please. lord. let him
be kind and handsome.

6
00:00:28.987 --> 00:00:31.156
And make room in my
heart for his children.

7
00:00:32.783 --> 00:00:35.994
I thought my time for
marriage had passed.

8
00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:38.455
but you had other plans.

9
00:00:43.502 --> 00:00:45.379
Today I begin a new life.

10
00:00:46.088 --> 00:00:48.257
I am to wed a leader.

11
00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:52.511
an explorer. the founder
of this island Hamlet.

12
00:00:53.637 --> 00:01:00.435
I. Sarah westcott. shall this day
become Mrs. Richard Warren.

13
00:01:02.312 --> 00:01:03.647
Just missed the fog.

14
00:01:04.272 --> 00:01:05.440
Stroke of luck. I suppose.

15
00:01:05.941 --> 00:01:08.151
No getting in or out once it arrives.

16
00:01:08.861 --> 00:01:09.981
Straight to the church then?

17
00:01:12.239 --> 00:01:13.591
What is he like?

18
00:01:13.615 --> 00:01:15.701
Well. he's the reason we're all here.

19
00:01:16.493 --> 00:01:18.653
Everyone on this island
owes a great debt to that man.

20
00:01:19.162 --> 00:01:22.433
Fore he arrived. it was a place
with nothing but barren dirt.

21
00:01:22.457 --> 00:01:27.045
But today. blossoms on the trees.
food for every hungry mouth. mild winters.

22
00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:29.798
He controls the weather. does he?

23
00:01:30.507 --> 00:01:31.508
What's that?

24
00:01:32.259 --> 00:01:33.886
He controls the weather. does he?

25
00:01:35.679 --> 00:01:36.763
No.

26
00:01:37.598 --> 00:01:40.910
But a cold breeze cuts half as quick

27
00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:43.562
when you've got a warm
home and a strong coat.

28
00:01:46.190 --> 00:01:47.191
Who said that?

29
00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:49.026
Richard Warren.

30
00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:57.074
Advertise your product or brand here
contact www.OpenSubtitles.org today

31
00:02:17.262 --> 00:02:19.264
Have you no kin come with you?

32
00:02:20.682 --> 00:02:21.683
No.

33
00:02:22.351 --> 00:02:24.686
I had resigned myself
to the lot of a spinster.

34
00:02:25.187 --> 00:02:29.667
Perhaps the greater celebration may be
me no longer a charge on my father's purse.

35
00:02:29.691 --> 00:02:33.362
It's a rare blessing to
marry at such an age.

36
00:02:34.238 --> 00:02:36.799
Lucky the island proved too
small to furnish him a wife.

37
00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:39.409
He had no choice but
to look to the mainland.

38
00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:43.997
A man of stature doth require a
goodly wife to order his household.

39
00:02:45.415 --> 00:02:47.626
Is he a man of-of good repute then?

40
00:02:53.006 --> 00:02:54.859
Sarah. my child.

41
00:02:54.883 --> 00:02:59.072
I am pastor Collins. Shepherd
of the flock here on this island.

42
00:02:59.096 --> 00:03:01.699
- Pleased to meet you. pastor.
- And I. you.

43
00:03:01.723 --> 00:03:02.951
How was your journey?

44
00:03:02.975 --> 00:03:06.287
Well. I… I arrived in good
order. for which I give thanks.

45
00:03:06.311 --> 00:03:10.399
It must seem to you a strange
land. and you a stranger in it.

46
00:03:10.941 --> 00:03:12.877
but know that you have friends here

47
00:03:12.901 --> 00:03:16.905
and the light of god to lift you
up whenever you feel alone.

48
00:03:18.532 --> 00:03:19.783
Thank you. pastor.

49
00:03:22.119 --> 00:03:27.350
If you are ever in need. do not
think twice to come to me at any hour.

50
00:03:27.374 --> 00:03:30.711
I will do what I can. by god's grace.

51
00:03:32.754 --> 00:03:34.006
I will. pastor.

52
00:03:35.132 --> 00:03:36.133
Good.

53
00:03:41.013 --> 00:03:44.391
Richard has requested to
be part of the wedding vows.

54
00:03:44.975 --> 00:03:47.144
Something he's written himself.

55
00:03:49.104 --> 00:03:51.523
They are unique.

56
00:03:53.609 --> 00:03:54.610
Unique?

57
00:03:56.195 --> 00:03:59.531
Love is as strong as death.

58
00:04:00.699 --> 00:04:05.972
Many waters cannot quench
love. neither can the floods drown it.

59
00:04:05.996 --> 00:04:09.750
Richard. do you take this
woman to be your lawful wife?

60
00:04:15.255 --> 00:04:16.440
I do.

61
00:04:16.464 --> 00:04:19.927
Sarah. do you take this
man as your lawful husband?

62
00:04:20.969 --> 00:04:23.263
- I do.
- For you. as his helpmeet.

63
00:04:23.847 --> 00:04:25.950
will be bound to him.

64
00:04:25.974 --> 00:04:30.038
You will agree to serve him as
the reeve prime of the colony.

65
00:04:30.062 --> 00:04:33.398
the handmaiden to
the lord island protector.

66
00:04:37.486 --> 00:04:38.820
I do. I do.

67
00:04:42.824 --> 00:04:48.681
Thomas. John. cromwell.
holyoke. Frances.

68
00:04:48.705 --> 00:04:50.517
Wagon wheel took her finger.

69
00:04:50.541 --> 00:04:52.876
Children. your new mother.

70
00:04:56.421 --> 00:04:58.340
'Tis a blessing to meet you all.

71
00:05:00.759 --> 00:05:01.760
Has she a name?

72
00:05:03.846 --> 00:05:04.888
Mary.

73
00:05:06.682 --> 00:05:07.683
Good name.

74
00:05:09.309 --> 00:05:10.978
But I think she's missing something.

75
00:05:15.649 --> 00:05:18.193
This brooch came from my mother.

76
00:05:21.196 --> 00:05:22.990
Is there one for each of us?

77
00:05:27.202 --> 00:05:30.372
Perhaps the morrow
shall yield further tokens.

78
00:05:35.502 --> 00:05:36.753
At such an hour?

79
00:05:44.678 --> 00:05:46.555
Ensure no harm comes to them.

80
00:05:48.807 --> 00:05:51.369
Have you an errand that
requires my company?

81
00:05:51.393 --> 00:05:53.395
No. I have work that needs doing.

82
00:05:55.731 --> 00:05:56.958
On our wedding night?

83
00:05:56.982 --> 00:06:00.003
The burdens of leadership ride
my shoulders by day and by dark.

84
00:06:00.027 --> 00:06:02.029
See them all laid down to their rest.

85
00:06:06.408 --> 00:06:10.245
I set down these lines for the
first time as a married woman.

86
00:06:10.787 --> 00:06:15.935
though I confess when my mother spoke
of what to expect on my wedding night.

87
00:06:15.959 --> 00:06:17.961
she missed the Mark.

88
00:06:19.004 --> 00:06:21.423
First. there are five children here.

89
00:06:22.174 --> 00:06:26.261
Second. my husband departed suddenly
with neither a caress nor a kind word.

90
00:06:27.471 --> 00:06:30.950
But Christ asks us not to despair.

91
00:06:30.974 --> 00:06:34.394
and I look with hope to
grow into the duties of a wife.

92
00:07:01.463 --> 00:07:02.464
Richard?

93
00:07:10.389 --> 00:07:11.640
Richard. are you home?

94
00:07:20.023 --> 00:07:21.108
Richard?

95
00:07:34.371 --> 00:07:35.372
Richard?

96
00:07:50.012 --> 00:07:51.096
Leave me be.

97
00:08:22.753 --> 00:08:24.171
You're a watcher.

98
00:08:28.967 --> 00:08:30.135
I'm sorry?

99
00:08:31.261 --> 00:08:33.323
You like to watch other people.

100
00:08:33.347 --> 00:08:35.349
see into their business.

101
00:08:36.850 --> 00:08:38.434
Forgive me. what befell them?

102
00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:41.145
There's a plague upon us.

103
00:08:41.647 --> 00:08:44.483
A violent madness
comes over the infected.

104
00:08:45.734 --> 00:08:47.069
Can they not be healed?

105
00:08:47.569 --> 00:08:49.029
Well. that's my husband.

106
00:08:49.738 --> 00:08:50.798
Town physician.

107
00:08:50.822 --> 00:08:52.199
He does what he can for them.

108
00:08:52.783 --> 00:08:54.761
gives them something
to calm their nerves.

109
00:08:54.785 --> 00:08:56.870
but heal them? No.

110
00:08:57.704 --> 00:08:58.705
But don't worry.

111
00:08:59.456 --> 00:09:03.460
Richard Warren always
says the bad times will end.

112
00:09:05.212 --> 00:09:06.839
God be with you.

113
00:09:08.924 --> 00:09:09.925
And with you.

114
00:09:17.099 --> 00:09:20.119
There's three more infected
this week since the fog.

115
00:09:20.143 --> 00:09:21.687
That makes 20 now in total.

116
00:09:23.063 --> 00:09:25.732
I have warned them to
stay out of the foul air.

117
00:09:26.233 --> 00:09:28.443
Otis Stevens tends to the sick every day.

118
00:09:29.778 --> 00:09:31.089
But he's not infected.

119
00:09:31.113 --> 00:09:32.614
Well. not yet.

120
00:09:33.532 --> 00:09:36.577
They say they suffer
from some kind of mania.

121
00:09:37.369 --> 00:09:38.662
Should we be worried?

122
00:09:40.455 --> 00:09:41.456
No.

123
00:09:44.710 --> 00:09:47.754
Cornelius Evans was the first to fall ill.

124
00:09:48.297 --> 00:09:50.132
At first. had no symptoms
beyond a headache.

125
00:09:50.841 --> 00:09:53.135
His wife gave him Brandy.
He slept soundly. but…

126
00:09:53.635 --> 00:09:57.264
He woke always with
the same headache. Here.

127
00:09:59.141 --> 00:10:00.684
Five days like this.

128
00:10:01.476 --> 00:10:03.371
And his eyes were
yellow with spoiled moons.

129
00:10:03.395 --> 00:10:04.455
He changed.

130
00:10:04.479 --> 00:10:06.040
He was angry. confused.

131
00:10:06.064 --> 00:10:07.292
Otis saw him that very night.

132
00:10:07.316 --> 00:10:08.710
He told him to take a warm bath.

133
00:10:08.734 --> 00:10:11.054
and he thought to come back
with a draught in the morning.

134
00:10:11.486 --> 00:10:13.906
But by dawn. when Otis came back.

135
00:10:14.823 --> 00:10:17.159
he saw a knot of hair in the doorway.

136
00:10:18.202 --> 00:10:22.206
Went inside and he found
Cornelius on the ground.

137
00:10:24.041 --> 00:10:26.752
With his fingers inside his wife's skull.

138
00:10:33.091 --> 00:10:35.093
The infections are growing faster.

139
00:10:35.677 --> 00:10:37.739
It will soon overwhelm us.

140
00:10:37.763 --> 00:10:39.157
We must do something.

141
00:10:39.181 --> 00:10:41.534
- You must do something.
- Sarah.

142
00:10:41.558 --> 00:10:43.894
would you take yourself to bed?

143
00:10:45.687 --> 00:10:47.189
But I haven't finished cleaning.

144
00:11:00.994 --> 00:11:03.556
They say that you're in
communion with this island.

145
00:11:03.580 --> 00:11:04.915
that you whisper to it.

146
00:11:05.707 --> 00:11:07.894
You tame it. You turn it to your will.

147
00:11:07.918 --> 00:11:10.438
That you are the only reason we survived

148
00:11:10.462 --> 00:11:12.816
- the first years.
- Hold your tongue.

149
00:11:12.840 --> 00:11:16.694
They say that you kiss that
necklace like it was a cross.

150
00:11:16.718 --> 00:11:18.136
but it's no cross. sir.

151
00:11:18.637 --> 00:11:20.323
What is it you hide in there?

152
00:11:20.347 --> 00:11:21.682
They say it is a covenant!

153
00:13:56.837 --> 00:13:58.630
Child. what ails thee?

154
00:14:06.722 --> 00:14:10.976
I feel I have greatly mistaken
my course in coming here.

155
00:14:13.812 --> 00:14:17.792
Though my days before were
sorrowful. I fared well enough.

156
00:14:17.816 --> 00:14:20.837
Perhaps the life of a… of a
childless woman without a husband.

157
00:14:20.861 --> 00:14:23.214
it is… it is… it is one I
could… I could come to bear…

158
00:14:23.238 --> 00:14:25.967
- Enj… enjoy! Enjoy the role...
- good woman. you are not making sense.

159
00:14:25.991 --> 00:14:28.493
Well. I am filled with terror. pastor!

160
00:14:29.036 --> 00:14:30.346
I saw him.

161
00:14:30.370 --> 00:14:33.040
I saw him murder Ezra Lowery.

162
00:14:34.625 --> 00:14:35.685
Is there a body?

163
00:14:35.709 --> 00:14:39.564
No. but there's a hidden
chamber beneath our home

164
00:14:39.588 --> 00:14:42.591
and Ezra's bloody cane therein.

165
00:14:44.218 --> 00:14:45.969
You must be told the truth.

166
00:14:47.554 --> 00:14:50.116
Evil stalks this land.

167
00:14:50.140 --> 00:14:52.142
There is a wrongness about.

168
00:14:53.769 --> 00:14:56.939
I fear that the devil himself
has chosen your husband.

169
00:14:57.523 --> 00:14:59.399
For what cause. I cannot tell.

170
00:15:00.317 --> 00:15:01.902
Others share my belief.

171
00:15:03.028 --> 00:15:04.780
We fear Warren consorts with him.

172
00:15:06.532 --> 00:15:08.700
Villagers go missing and
they're never seen again.

173
00:15:09.284 --> 00:15:10.720
including his last wife.

174
00:15:10.744 --> 00:15:11.912
God.

175
00:15:12.955 --> 00:15:16.768
I cannot stay here a moment
longer. I want off this dreadful island.

176
00:15:16.792 --> 00:15:20.188
I am but four and ten years almost.
Allow me to wither in my father's attic…

177
00:15:20.212 --> 00:15:22.106
- Sarah. Sarah.
- …As my womanly destiny.

178
00:15:22.130 --> 00:15:23.131
Sarah.

179
00:15:25.133 --> 00:15:28.887
Know that god has chosen
you for a special purpose.

180
00:15:30.097 --> 00:15:33.785
You arrived on this island
not for the reason you thought.

181
00:15:33.809 --> 00:15:35.811
but for a greater one still.

182
00:15:36.395 --> 00:15:39.231
Thou art not alone.

183
00:15:41.149 --> 00:15:43.652
When you retire to bed tonight.

184
00:15:45.070 --> 00:15:48.657
leave the front door
unlatched so that we may enter.

185
00:15:49.783 --> 00:15:50.784
To do what?

186
00:15:53.537 --> 00:15:55.372
What must be done.

187
00:15:59.668 --> 00:16:04.047
No one understands
the burdens of leadership.

188
00:16:04.673 --> 00:16:07.443
They're conspiring against
me. and you know that.

189
00:16:07.467 --> 00:16:10.446
They are afraid. The
plague. the disappearances…

190
00:16:10.470 --> 00:16:11.763
Disappearances?

191
00:16:14.641 --> 00:16:15.893
What disappearances?

192
00:16:18.562 --> 00:16:20.081
Who have you been speaking with?

193
00:16:20.105 --> 00:16:21.315
I've spoken with no one.

194
00:16:25.235 --> 00:16:26.296
'Tis nothing.

195
00:16:28.322 --> 00:16:30.884
Forgive me. I cannot
make sense of my own…

196
00:16:30.908 --> 00:16:31.992
My own words.

197
00:16:34.953 --> 00:16:36.622
Take all the children upstairs.

198
00:16:37.539 --> 00:16:38.540
The…

199
00:16:39.166 --> 00:16:40.167
Children.

200
00:16:53.722 --> 00:16:55.140
Is something wrong?

201
00:16:58.852 --> 00:17:00.270
All shall be well.

202
00:19:45.811 --> 00:19:47.813
Did I not plainly forewarn you?

203
00:19:50.023 --> 00:19:52.526
For your own safety. you
must not leave this house again.

204
00:19:53.485 --> 00:19:55.904
Not to do the wash. not
to accompany the children.

205
00:20:01.702 --> 00:20:05.038
Well. let no fear take hold.

206
00:20:06.707 --> 00:20:10.520
I will unearth the one
who bears this guilt.

207
00:20:10.544 --> 00:20:15.966
None may hide forever on an
island where there is no way out.

208
00:20:21.263 --> 00:20:22.431
I will protect us.

209
00:20:28.645 --> 00:20:29.646
Go to our room.

210
00:20:30.480 --> 00:20:31.690
Pray.

211
00:20:42.868 --> 00:20:46.330
Please. Please. Father. please.

212
00:20:49.041 --> 00:20:50.042
Please.

213
00:24:22.963 --> 00:24:24.214
Pastor Collins!

214
00:24:25.340 --> 00:24:27.968
Richard is alive!

215
00:24:30.846 --> 00:24:33.724
Yes. we noted that with some distress.

216
00:24:35.434 --> 00:24:37.829
Be not afraid. This
committee can be trusted.

217
00:24:37.853 --> 00:24:39.664
Then you all must listen.

218
00:24:39.688 --> 00:24:41.583
He is not consorting with the devil.

219
00:24:41.607 --> 00:24:43.084
He is the devil.

220
00:24:43.108 --> 00:24:46.004
I saw him struck with a knife
again and again. but he died not.

221
00:24:46.028 --> 00:24:48.923
For the good of every man. woman.
and child. you must make haste

222
00:24:48.947 --> 00:24:50.490
and stop him immediately.

223
00:24:53.243 --> 00:24:54.971
There's a secret tunnel
that leads to the house.

224
00:24:54.995 --> 00:24:58.308
There's a well at the far southeastern
edge that will Grant to serve you passage.

225
00:24:58.332 --> 00:25:00.834
You must send ten good. strong men.

226
00:25:05.672 --> 00:25:08.985
A merchant sailing vessel
is due to depart this evening

227
00:25:09.009 --> 00:25:12.322
with a berth for you
on it… god be thanked.

228
00:25:12.346 --> 00:25:15.265
…but we need your help.

229
00:25:19.061 --> 00:25:24.626
Pour this in his drink. and
he will be helpless as a babe.

230
00:25:24.650 --> 00:25:26.711
No. I cannot go back there.

231
00:25:26.735 --> 00:25:29.488
You must. or he shall know.

232
00:25:30.364 --> 00:25:35.261
You said he must be stopped.
Now you bear the burden as well.

233
00:25:35.285 --> 00:25:38.121
Consider the welfare of your children.

234
00:25:39.289 --> 00:25:42.769
My children? I have but just met them.

235
00:25:42.793 --> 00:25:44.795
Sarah. please.

236
00:25:45.337 --> 00:25:49.174
You are our only hope
against this darkness.

237
00:25:54.555 --> 00:25:57.867
I do not comprehend
the nature of the curse

238
00:25:57.891 --> 00:25:59.643
that has fallen on the island.

239
00:26:00.435 --> 00:26:06.608
I do know that its heart beats inside the
cylinder my husband wears around his neck.

240
00:26:07.359 --> 00:26:08.837
Who will crush my throat?

241
00:26:08.861 --> 00:26:11.965
His hands? This plague?

242
00:26:11.989 --> 00:26:15.993
Death comes for us
each. but I fear to me first.

243
00:26:16.785 --> 00:26:18.620
I know not how. but who.

244
00:26:28.505 --> 00:26:33.427
Of course. he's here with
me. so I say all this in jest.

245
00:26:34.011 --> 00:26:36.096
And with that. I retire.

246
00:26:46.481 --> 00:26:48.066
You're home. What a blessing.

247
00:26:49.735 --> 00:26:51.778
What do you write in that book?

248
00:26:53.071 --> 00:26:54.781
A woman's silly thoughts.

249
00:26:56.700 --> 00:26:57.951
I want to read it.

250
00:26:59.244 --> 00:27:00.829
I would feel too abashed.

251
00:27:28.315 --> 00:27:30.317
A swig of Brandy to ease your mind.

252
00:27:32.194 --> 00:27:34.112
No. I need to be clearheaded.

253
00:27:41.537 --> 00:27:42.972
Go to your beds now. children.

254
00:27:42.996 --> 00:27:46.083
Now. I need a quiet
word with your father.

255
00:27:47.668 --> 00:27:48.669
Now.

256
00:28:05.853 --> 00:28:11.775
If folk are truly set against you.
you need your wife at your side.

257
00:28:15.904 --> 00:28:18.365
We are married all these
days and have not yet…

258
00:28:21.285 --> 00:28:22.452
Known each other.

259
00:28:28.333 --> 00:28:32.856
Well. the burdens that
have been placed upon me...

260
00:28:32.880 --> 00:28:34.882
let me help you bear them.

261
00:29:08.040 --> 00:29:09.958
What sin lies on your tongue?

262
00:29:12.961 --> 00:29:16.089
You're in league with them. Traitress.

263
00:29:31.563 --> 00:29:32.731
He killed my mother.

264
00:29:35.025 --> 00:29:36.944
Gather your siblings. We're leaving.

265
00:29:44.201 --> 00:29:45.512
Who are they?

266
00:29:45.536 --> 00:29:46.703
Just keep moving.

267
00:30:09.434 --> 00:30:10.644
They left without us.

268
00:30:11.854 --> 00:30:14.273
Here. into this boat. We can catch them.

269
00:30:14.982 --> 00:30:15.983
Easy.

270
00:30:23.365 --> 00:30:24.908
Are you leaving?

271
00:30:27.202 --> 00:30:28.412
Abigail. I…

272
00:30:29.454 --> 00:30:31.290
I reckon you are not well.

273
00:30:31.957 --> 00:30:33.584
Go to your husband. the physician.

274
00:30:34.585 --> 00:30:35.794
I did already.

275
00:30:39.464 --> 00:30:41.317
I will get on board with you.

276
00:30:41.341 --> 00:30:43.427
I'm sorry. there is not enough space.

277
00:30:45.095 --> 00:30:46.680
But I am not sick!

278
00:30:48.557 --> 00:30:50.142
Forgive me. there is no space.

279
00:30:50.684 --> 00:30:53.520
Then leave off these children.
They're not of thy blood.

280
00:30:56.064 --> 00:30:57.065
They're with me.

281
00:30:59.526 --> 00:31:01.069
And under my charge.

282
00:31:03.780 --> 00:31:07.451
Stand back! I will take no more orders!

283
00:31:18.295 --> 00:31:21.381
Go. Go. The ropes.

284
00:31:35.896 --> 00:31:37.022
Traitors.

285
00:31:40.234 --> 00:31:44.130
You've set yourself above
the law of god and man.

286
00:31:44.154 --> 00:31:48.158
You have murdered
those you swore to protect.

287
00:31:49.368 --> 00:31:50.369
No!

288
00:31:51.036 --> 00:31:53.223
It doesn't want you to open it.

289
00:31:53.247 --> 00:31:55.791
What does not want me to open it?

290
00:31:56.375 --> 00:31:58.126
That which has kept us alive.

291
00:31:59.127 --> 00:32:03.024
It is just as we feared. You
have made a deal with the devil.

292
00:32:03.048 --> 00:32:05.217
No. it's not the devil.

293
00:32:05.843 --> 00:32:07.487
It is our god.

294
00:32:07.511 --> 00:32:10.990
He's gone mad. Let us be rid of him.

295
00:32:11.014 --> 00:32:12.516
You cannot rid yourself of me.

296
00:32:13.517 --> 00:32:15.078
It won't allow it.

297
00:32:15.102 --> 00:32:17.521
This is my burden.

298
00:32:18.438 --> 00:32:23.461
Free me. you will all be forgiven.
and I will continue to carry it myself.

299
00:32:23.485 --> 00:32:29.199
Your fate will be decided
by god. the one true god.

300
00:32:37.040 --> 00:32:42.004
No. You cannot Bury
me! You cannot Bury me!

301
00:32:43.380 --> 00:32:45.883
You'll doom yourselves! The pact!

302
00:32:46.383 --> 00:32:48.278
The pact must be honored!

303
00:32:48.302 --> 00:32:51.847
The pact which spared
us… in that first winter.

304
00:32:52.431 --> 00:32:55.017
It spoke to me through the mushrooms!

305
00:32:56.101 --> 00:32:58.413
Please. Fulfill the pact.

306
00:32:58.437 --> 00:32:59.706
How?

307
00:32:59.730 --> 00:33:02.858
Sacrifice! A life… life for life.

308
00:33:04.276 --> 00:33:09.448
Whatever I have undertaken. it has
been for the welfare of our people!

309
00:33:10.282 --> 00:33:14.953
Fulfill the pact and the plague will stop!

310
00:33:15.913 --> 00:33:17.122
But if you don't…

311
00:33:17.706 --> 00:33:18.832
If you do not.

312
00:33:20.417 --> 00:33:22.604
the terrors will not cease!

313
00:33:22.628 --> 00:33:24.314
They will only deepen!

314
00:33:24.338 --> 00:33:28.383
Please do not make my
children suffer for your mistake.

315
00:33:29.051 --> 00:33:33.055
Your wife is taking your children
back to the mainland. far from you.

316
00:33:34.848 --> 00:33:37.285
No. No. no. no.

317
00:33:37.309 --> 00:33:39.645
The island won't… the
island won't let them leave.

318
00:33:40.562 --> 00:33:42.373
Please! Please!

319
00:33:42.397 --> 00:33:44.441
You'll kill them all! You'll kill them all!

320
00:33:48.820 --> 00:33:56.262
You'll kill them all! You'll kill them all!

321
00:33:56.286 --> 00:33:58.330
You'll kill them all!

322
00:33:58.997 --> 00:34:03.812
You'll kill them all! You'll kill them all!

323
00:34:03.836 --> 00:34:07.005
You'll kill them all!

324
00:35:23.332 --> 00:35:24.333
I got it.

325
00:35:27.920 --> 00:35:29.505
- You got it?
- Come on.

325
00:35:30.305 --> 00:36:30.371
